+# Design: Move off request
+
+Ecosystem: JavaScript / TypeScript (CommonJS, Node `>=18`). Version in use: `request@2.88.2` (lockfile).
+
+## Approach
+
+Replace the two `request` calls in `src/rates.js` with a project-owned module `src/vendor/request-lite.js` built on the platform `fetch`. No package is added. The module keeps the parts of `request` the project uses: `qs` serialisation, `json: true` / `json: <body>`, `timeout`, redirect policy, and the `(err, res, body)` result shape. `getRate` and `archiveReceipt` keep their signatures.
+
+## The séance (differential test)
+
+Both implementations are loaded in one test file (fast-check with Vitest). For each API from the inventory the test:
+
+1. builds an arbitrary that generates inputs of the types the API accepts, biased toward edge cases (empty, zero, negative, very long, unicode, `null` and `undefined`);
+2. calls `request` and `fetch` with the same input;
+3. fails if the results differ, or if exactly one of them throws, and shows the shrunk input and both outputs.
+
+While `request` is still installed, it is the oracle. Before it is removed, record its outputs for the failing and edge inputs as a golden file, so the test keeps guarding the new code.
+
+## Risks
+
+- A behaviour that the inventory missed. The test only covers the APIs it lists.
+- Differences the project relies on by accident (error messages, key order). Decide per case whether to match or to change the caller.
+- A runtime that lacks the platform API. Check the supported runtime list first (`engines.node >=18`: `fetch` is present).
+- Known places where `request` and bare `fetch` differ (to be confirmed by the séance, not assumed): query encoding (`qs` versus `URLSearchParams`), POST redirects, `json: true` leaving an unparsable body as a string and an empty body as `undefined`, and the meaning of `timeout` (socket idle time versus a total deadline).
+
+## Order of work
+
+Inventory, then the séance against the old code, then the switch, then the removal.
+
+## The séance
+
+No curated recipe exists for this pair, so the generic template wrote the skeleton. Every `TODO(necromancer)` marker is a decision it could not make; the comparisons stay skipped until the replacement is written and `READY` is set. The project-specific parts are written by hand (see the séance README).
+
+Files to add to the project:
+
+- `seance/request/seance.test.mjs` (test)
+- `seance/request/replacement.mjs` (replacement)
+- `seance/request/README.md` (readme)
+
+Install and run:
+
+```sh
+npm install --save-dev vitest fast-check request
+npx vitest run seance/request
+```
+
+What it compares and ignores:
+
+- The returned value, or the error class when the call throws (never the message).
+- Members the project calls: default, post.
+- Inputs: the project's own literal calls, plus generated arguments. Generators marked TODO(necromancer) are guesses.
+
+## Known behavioural differences
+
+_(to be filled in from the séance results; empty until the séance has run)_
