+// paired with a server that answers later than it, and an immediate answer only with a long or no timeout.
+// A timeout under 50 ms is left out: in request it also covers the connection, so the answer depends on
+// how fast the socket connects (old versus old fails on it, with ETIMEDOUT instead of ESOCKETTIMEDOUT).
+// Negative timeouts are left out: request's own answer depends on whether the connection is new (a 0 ms
+// connect timer races it) or reused (the timeout is ignored), so the oracle is not deterministic.
