+// request-lite: the part of the `request` package this project uses, on the platform `fetch`.
+// It keeps request's contract for: url, qs, headers, json, timeout, the (err, res, body) callback,
+// GET redirects and the error codes. Anything else request accepted is refused with a TypeError
+// instead of being ignored. The differences that were looked at and accepted are listed in
+// .kiro/specs/migrate-off-request/design.md ("Known behavioural differences") and asserted by
+// seance/request/seance.test.mjs.
+//
+// Parts ported from request's own dependencies, so the bytes on the wire stay the same:
+//   - qs@6.5.5 `stringify`/`utils.encode` (BSD-3-Clause), for primitive values only
+//   - json-stringify-safe@5.0.1 (ISC)
